$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Secondary (Norton) creep, single element, constant load  --  MSC Nastran SOL 400
$
$   units : mm - N - tonne - s   (stress MPa)
$   model : 1 x 1 x 1 mm CHEXA, 1/8 symmetry, 100 N pulled on the x=1 face
$           -> sigma_x = 100 MPa held for 1000 s
$   law   : Norton   eps_dot_cr = A * sigma^M ,  A = 1e-15, M = 5
$   check : creep strain after 1000 s = 0.01000, total ux = 0.0104762 mm
$
$   MATVP primary format is   MATVP MID A IT3D M N P Q IUSER   where the law is
$       eps_dot_cr = A * sigma^M * eps^N * t^P   (Q is the temperature term)
$   so Norton is M=5 with N=P=Q=0.  IT3D=0 means "no TABL3D, use the exponents".
$
$   TWO THINGS THE QRG IS EXPLICIT ABOUT AND BOTH BITE:
$     1. "Creep analysis requires an initial static solution at t = 0, which can
$        be obtained by specifying a subcase that requests an NLPARM entry with
$        DT = 0.0."   -> SUBCASE 1 below does exactly that.
$     2. "In SOL 400, MATVP is only supported for elements with property
$        extensions" -- PSOLID must be paired with PSLDN1, same as MATS1 needs
$        it for large strain.  Without it the creep data is not used.
$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SOL 400
CEND
TITLE    = Norton creep 1-element, constant 100 MPa (mm-N-tonne-s)
ECHO     = NONE
$
$ SUBCASE 1 : t = 0 static solution (NLPARM with DT = 0.0)
SUBCASE 1
  LABEL = apply 100 N, no creep time
  ANALYSIS     = NLSTATICS
  SPC          = 1
  LOAD         = 2
  NLPARM       = 10
  DISPLACEMENT(PLOT) = ALL
  STRESS(PLOT)       = ALL
  SPCFORCES(PLOT)    = ALL
$
$ SUBCASE 2 : hold the same load for 1000 s and creep
SUBCASE 2
  LABEL = hold 1000 s
  ANALYSIS     = NLSTATICS
  SPC          = 1
  LOAD         = 2
  NLPARM       = 20
  DISPLACEMENT(PLOT) = ALL
  STRESS(PLOT)       = ALL
  STRAIN(PLOT)       = ALL
$
BEGIN BULK
$
PARAM,POST,-1
$
$ DT = 0.0 -> the t=0 static solution the QRG asks for
$       ID      NINC    DT      KMETHOD KSTEP   MAXITER CONV    INTOUT
NLPARM  10      1       0.0     FNT     5       25      PW      YES
$ 100 increments of 10 s = 1000 s of creep
NLPARM  20      100     10.0    FNT     5       25      PW      YES
$
$===============================================================================
$ MESH
$===============================================================================
$       ID                      X       Y       Z
GRID    1               0.0     0.0     0.0
GRID    2               1.0     0.0     0.0
GRID    3               1.0     1.0     0.0
GRID    4               0.0     1.0     0.0
GRID    5               0.0     0.0     1.0
GRID    6               1.0     0.0     1.0
GRID    7               1.0     1.0     1.0
GRID    8               0.0     1.0     1.0
$
$       EID     PID     G1      G2      G3      G4      G5      G6
CHEXA   1       1       1       2       3       4       5       6
+       7       8
$
$       PID     MID     CORDM
PSOLID  1       1       0
$ property extension -- MATVP needs it in SOL 400
PSLDN1  1       1
+       C8      SOLID   L
$
$===============================================================================
$ MATERIAL
$===============================================================================
$       MID     E       G       NU      RHO
MAT1    1       210000.         0.3     7.85-9
$
$       MID     A       IT3D    M       N       P       Q       IUSER
MATVP   1       1.0-15  0       5.0     0.0     0.0     0.0
$
$===============================================================================
$ BOUNDARY CONDITIONS AND LOAD
$===============================================================================
$       SID     C       G1      G2      G3      G4
SPC1    1       1       1       4       5       8
SPC1    1       2       1       2       5       6
SPC1    1       3       1       2       3       4
$
$ 4 nodes x 25 N = 100 N over 1 mm2 = 100 MPa
$       SID     G       CID     F       N1      N2      N3
FORCE   2       2       0       25.0    1.0     0.0     0.0
FORCE   2       3       0       25.0    1.0     0.0     0.0
FORCE   2       6       0       25.0    1.0     0.0     0.0
FORCE   2       7       0       25.0    1.0     0.0     0.0
$
ENDDATA
